From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:54:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 45/47] minimize: pin an app to a workspace from the window
 menu
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The window menu gets one entry for Workspace Keeper: "Always open on
“<workspace>”" pins the app to the workspace its window is on, and
"Stop opening on “<workspace>”" removes the pin. The entry is hidden
when the window has no app id or Workspace Keeper is not installed
(~/.local/bin/ws-keeper).

Pins live in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ws-keeper/pins, one `app_id = Workspace`
rule per line; Workspace Keeper reads the file and moves the windows.
The applet only edits it: the app's rules are replaced or removed, all
other lines and comments are kept, and the file is written through a
temporary file and a rename. Parsing follows Workspace Keeper (split at
the first `=`, last rule wins, rules without a name skipped, a byte
order mark ignored).

Items of pinned apps show a small pin on the top right of their icon
(top/bottom panel, only with Workspace Keeper installed and a
pin-symbolic icon in the theme). The file is re-read every 2 s when it
changed, and at once after the menu wrote it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

